# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm POST Object parses If-Match/If-None-Match and exposes those values to bucket policy authorization.
- [x] Confirm the parsed WriteCondition is not retained in StreamingPostContext.
- [x] Confirm POST finalization passes WriteCondition::default() to storage commit while storage has enforcement for non-default conditions.
- [x] Dynamically reproduce policy behavior: POST without If-None-Match is denied while POST with If-None-Match:* is authorized.
- [x] Dynamically reproduce commit bypass: a second POST with If-None-Match:* to an existing key succeeds and overwrites the object; also attempted crash/Valgrind/ASan/debugger workflow and captured LLDB trace.
## Report
Validated the suspected authorization/commit mismatch at commit 67175e5b94e6b60937f6352515d0952dc1ea66ff. Code review showed POST Object parses conditional headers at crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:3476 and puts those values into PutObjectPolicyContext at lines 3495-3501, so bucket policy evaluation sees s3:if-match / s3:if-none-match. However StreamingPostContext at lines 3532-3545 does not store the parsed WriteCondition. During POST finalization, crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:3586-3595 calls finalize_authorized_stream_put with cond: &WriteCondition::default(), making the storage commit unconditional. The enforcement that should reject If-None-Match:* overwrites exists in crates/server-core/src/conditional.rs:255-276, and streaming commit only invokes it when cond is non-empty in crates/server-core/src/coordinator/put.rs:533-545.

Dynamic PoC: I added a targeted integration test that creates a bucket policy denying PutObject when s3:if-none-match is null. The PoC output was: no If-None-Match POST: status=403 with AccessDenied; first If-None-Match:* POST: status=204; repeat If-None-Match:* POST to the same key: status=204; final object body="overwrite". A correct implementation should reject the repeat create-only write with 412 once the object exists. Command used: RUST_BACKTRACE=1 cargo test -p s3-tests --test validation_post_if_none_match_poc -- --nocapture.

Crash/Valgrind/ASan/debugger attempts: this is a logic bug, so no crash was expected or observed. valgrind was unavailable in the container (bash: command not found: valgrind). ASan for Rust required nightly; nightly download failed due blocked network, and stable rejected -Z sanitizer=address. I then used LLDB non-interactively. The debugger trace stopped in HttpFrontend::finalize_streaming_post_object at mod.rs:3586, then in Coordinator::finalize_authorized_stream_put with the stack showing the call originated from finalize_streaming_post_object. The source at that call site constructs the request with cond: &WriteCondition::default() at mod.rs:3594, confirming the POST path reaches storage finalization without the If-None-Match condition that was used for policy authorization.

